LionClip for Debian/Ubuntu/Zorin
================================

What the package installs
-------------------------

  /usr/bin/lionclip                                       the application
  /usr/bin/lionclip-shortcut                              Super+V setup helper
  /usr/share/applications/…LionClip.desktop               app launcher entry
  /etc/xdg/autostart/…LionClip.desktop                    starts it at login
  /usr/share/icons/hicolor/…/apps/…LionClip.{svg,png}     icon
  /usr/share/metainfo/…LionClip.metainfo.xml              AppStream metadata

Autostart
---------

The autostart entry runs `lionclip`, which starts the resident instance and its
clipboard monitor without opening the popup. Disable it per user with:

    mkdir -p ~/.config/autostart
    cp /etc/xdg/autostart/io.github.Pianisuto.LionClip.desktop ~/.config/autostart/
    sed -i 's/^X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=true/X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=false/' \
        ~/.config/autostart/io.github.Pianisuto.LionClip.desktop

Remove that copy to enable it again. GNOME Tweaks writes the same file.

Super+V
-------

    lionclip-shortcut install     bind Super+V to `lionclip toggle`
    lionclip-shortcut status      show what Super+V is bound to
    lionclip-shortcut remove      undo it

Your clipboard history
----------------------

The history lives in $XDG_DATA_HOME/lionclip (usually ~/.local/share/lionclip)
and belongs to you: removing or purging the package never deletes it. To delete
it yourself:

    rm -rf ~/.local/share/lionclip

Upgrades
--------

Installing a new version replaces the binary on disk but does not restart a
LionClip that is already running. Log out and back in, or restart it with:

    pkill -x lionclip && setsid lionclip >/dev/null 2>&1 &
